<article class="env-lemma" id="0C2S">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C2S">Lemma <span data-tag="0C2S">55.8.1</span>.</a> Let $V_1 \to V_2$ be a closed immersion of algebraic schemes over $K$. If $X_2$ is a model for $V_2$, then the scheme theoretic image of $V_1 \to X_2$ is a model for $V_1$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Using Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01R8" data-tag="01R8">29.6.3</a> and Example <a href="/tag/056A" data-tag="056A">29.6.4</a> this boils down to the following algebra statement. Let $A_1$ be a finite type $R$-algebra flat over $R$. Let $A_1 \otimes _ R K \to B_2$ be a surjection. Then $A_2 = A_1 / \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(A_1 \to B_2)$ is a finite type $R$-algebra flat over $R$ such that $B_2 = A_2 \otimes _ R K$. We omit the detailed proof; use More on Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/0AUW" data-tag="0AUW">15.22.11</a> to prove that $A_2$ is flat. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>